WEBVTT

00:00.520 --> 00:03.880
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.881 --> 00:07.181
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.182 --> 00:10.751
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.752 --> 00:13.754
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.755 --> 00:17.258
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.259 --> 00:20.595
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.596 --> 00:22.129
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.130 --> 00:23.497
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.498 --> 00:29.086
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.361 --> 00:37.545
I got to say, some days I wish

00:37.546 --> 00:39.447
I didn't have a sister.

00:39.448 --> 00:42.149
Oh...

00:42.150 --> 00:43.384
- What?
- Nothing.

00:43.385 --> 00:44.719
Oh, I thought you asked me

00:44.720 --> 00:46.254
what was going on with my sister.

00:46.255 --> 00:49.290
I did not.

00:49.291 --> 00:50.992
Hey, look. Tom Tucker.

00:50.993 --> 00:52.326
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker.

00:52.327 --> 00:54.462
Coming up, tonight's second story.

00:54.463 --> 00:56.530
But first, Quahog says good-bye

00:56.531 --> 00:57.798
to an old friend.

00:57.799 --> 00:59.800
That's right, Tom. Medieval Castle,

00:59.801 --> 01:02.169
which has been a staple of
family entertainment and dining,

01:02.170 --> 01:03.537
is closing its doors.

01:03.538 --> 01:05.373
The restaurant has
gone into foreclosure,

01:05.374 --> 01:07.408
and will be up for auction tomorrow.

01:07.409 --> 01:09.777
Yes, hard to believe a place
where you eat with your hands

01:09.778 --> 01:11.245
next to piles of horse dung

01:11.246 --> 01:13.080
while untrained theater students fight

01:13.081 --> 01:15.750
with real swords could
be drowning in lawsuits.

01:15.751 --> 01:17.752
Medieval Castle? I love that place.

01:17.753 --> 01:19.600
My sister almost got a job there once.

01:19.601 --> 01:22.156
Guys, we should go to that
auction tomorrow and buy it.

01:22.157 --> 01:25.126
I mean, can you imagine if we
had our own medieval castle?

01:25.127 --> 01:26.160
I bet it'd be even more fun

01:26.161 --> 01:28.012
than when I went to White Castle.

01:30.283 --> 01:33.751
Huh. Name's a little deceiving.

01:40.976 --> 01:42.043
What's wrong with you?

01:42.044 --> 01:44.045
Oh, it's my back. It's killing me.

01:44.046 --> 01:46.647
Yeah, I'm not falling for that
hot-oil massage bit again.

01:46.648 --> 01:47.906
No, this time it's not a bit.

01:47.907 --> 01:49.219
I'm really hurt.

01:49.220 --> 01:51.250
I must have jacked it up playing sports

01:51.251 --> 01:53.552
and not trying to dance like Beyoncé.

01:53.553 --> 01:54.786
Wow. If you're in that much pain,

01:54.787 --> 01:55.821
I better tell Lois.

01:55.822 --> 01:57.289
Please don't.

01:57.290 --> 01:58.757
Then she'll drive me to the doctor,

01:58.758 --> 02:00.859
and I hate being in the car with her.

02:00.860 --> 02:03.895
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

02:03.896 --> 02:07.232
♪ Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh ♪
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

02:07.233 --> 02:09.601
♪ Shut the door, baby,
don't say a word ♪

02:09.602 --> 02:12.871
<i>Okay, I guess that's not my part.</i>

02:15.942 --> 02:18.477
There it is, guys. Aw,
this is gonna be awesome!

02:18.478 --> 02:19.845
We just got to win this auction,

02:19.846 --> 02:21.480
and then we'll have our own castle.

02:21.481 --> 02:24.716
Oh, yeah? Over my dead tooth!

02:24.717 --> 02:26.952
Good afternoon, and welcome
to today's auction.

02:26.953 --> 02:28.520
I'm Al Harrington, of Al Harrington's

02:28.521 --> 02:30.122
Wacky Waving Inflatable Arm-Flailing

02:30.123 --> 02:31.857
Tubeman Warehouse and Emporium.

02:31.858 --> 02:33.325
Due to the presence of black mold,

02:33.326 --> 02:34.993
discarded half-eaten turkey legs,

02:34.994 --> 02:37.696
and an undulating rat king
that no one dares approach,

02:37.697 --> 02:40.032
I have been advised to move
these proceedings along

02:40.033 --> 02:41.366
as quickly as possible.

02:41.367 --> 02:43.402
Do I hear an opening bid? Anyone.

02:43.403 --> 02:45.604
Do I hear an opening
bid for this majestic

02:45.605 --> 02:47.039
fiberglass castle facade,

02:47.040 --> 02:49.474
masking what was once
a Midas Muffler shop?

02:49.475 --> 02:50.642
Two bits.

02:50.643 --> 02:53.078
Two bits. That's 25
cents in the Old West.

02:53.079 --> 02:56.515
We have 25 cents. Do I
hear higher than 25 cents?

02:56.516 --> 02:59.718
This paper bag, which could
be full of money or my socks.

02:59.719 --> 03:00.952
You take the chance.

03:00.953 --> 03:02.754
We have an intriguing mystery bag.

03:02.755 --> 03:04.890
Do I hear more than the mystery bag?

03:04.891 --> 03:06.925
Two bits and a cardboard box,

03:06.926 --> 03:10.295
which may or may not
contain a mystery bag.

03:10.296 --> 03:12.030
Already the most challenging auction

03:12.031 --> 03:13.332
I have ever been a part of.

03:13.333 --> 03:14.633
Do I hear a higher bid

03:14.634 --> 03:16.802
from that James Bond villain over there?

03:16.803 --> 03:19.738
50 kroner.

03:19.739 --> 03:21.440
Which, converted to American currency,

03:21.441 --> 03:23.108
is $7.40.

03:23.109 --> 03:26.244
Do I hear a much higher bid,
followed by shocked murmuring?

03:26.245 --> 03:28.747
$10,000!

03:28.748 --> 03:30.264
- I'm shocked.
- That's shocking.

03:30.265 --> 03:31.617
We're all shocked.

03:31.618 --> 03:33.085
We can't afford that.

03:33.086 --> 03:34.886
Peter, do something. I can't.

03:34.887 --> 03:37.656
There's only $9,000 in the mystery bag.

03:37.657 --> 03:39.358
Due to my 12:00 noon court appointment

03:39.359 --> 03:41.259
as part of a crippling
child-custody battle

03:41.260 --> 03:42.761
with my horrific ex-wife,

03:42.762 --> 03:45.063
I am saying going once, going twice,

03:45.064 --> 03:48.834
and awarding this condemned
building to you...!

03:50.436 --> 03:51.703
Damn, it, we lost!

03:51.704 --> 03:54.239
I guess the castle was
a crazy idea anyway.

03:54.240 --> 03:55.841
I should probably just invest this money

03:55.842 --> 03:57.492
in a 401-Gay.

03:58.962 --> 04:01.042
And how long before I can take this out?

04:05.702 --> 04:08.487
Man, those losers don't
deserve that castle.

04:08.488 --> 04:10.655
I would call my sister about this

04:10.656 --> 04:12.724
if she were able to answer the phone.

04:12.725 --> 04:15.360
Poor thing.

04:15.361 --> 04:16.661
Poor, poor thing.

04:16.662 --> 04:19.164
Well, you know, in castle times,

04:19.165 --> 04:20.866
if you wanted something,
you just took it.

04:20.867 --> 04:22.033
What are you talking about?

04:22.034 --> 04:24.603
I'm saying the four of us
should storm that castle

04:24.604 --> 04:25.971
and take it for ourselves.

04:25.972 --> 04:27.706
Should we do it with careful planning,

04:27.707 --> 04:30.475
or have another couple beers
and then just go for it?

04:30.476 --> 04:31.643
Well, let's make that decision

04:31.644 --> 04:33.595
after another couple beers.

04:38.635 --> 04:40.752
I checked with my mom, and she said

04:40.753 --> 04:43.989
it was cool with her if we
wanted to sleep here tonight.

04:43.990 --> 04:46.091
- I'm pretty sure I can.
- Count me in.

04:46.092 --> 04:49.043
I'm gonna have to go
home and get my pillow.

04:53.466 --> 04:56.601
Yes, you heard me right,
cancel my insurance.

04:56.602 --> 04:59.070
I've been in this location for 40 years,

04:59.071 --> 05:01.273
and never once have I broken a lamp.

05:01.274 --> 05:02.991
Good day, sir.

05:06.563 --> 05:09.214
God, I hope he's got insurance.

05:09.215 --> 05:10.415
Of course he's got insurance.

05:10.416 --> 05:12.534
He's been at this location for 40 years.

05:15.238 --> 05:16.755
Yes, you heard me right.

05:16.756 --> 05:18.623
Cancel my husband's life insurance.

05:18.624 --> 05:20.759
He's been in perfect
health for 40 years.

05:20.760 --> 05:23.295
We're selling the lamp
store and going to travel.

05:23.296 --> 05:25.831
We need this after losing
both our children.

05:25.832 --> 05:27.599
Good day, sir.

05:31.288 --> 05:32.871
All right, plan "B."

05:32.872 --> 05:35.440
<i>We'll shoot flaming arrows,
like in Robin Hood.</i>

05:35.441 --> 05:38.009
So should I be aiming
for an open window,

05:38.010 --> 05:39.611
or just arcing it over the wall?

05:39.612 --> 05:40.946
I don't know, I've never seen the movie,

05:40.947 --> 05:42.414
just the Bryan Adams video.

05:42.415 --> 05:43.949
Oh, such a good song.

05:43.950 --> 05:44.950
Archers...

05:44.951 --> 05:46.117
Yeah?

05:46.118 --> 05:47.752
Oh, yeah, he's that guy, too.

05:47.753 --> 05:49.537
Prepare to fire.

05:58.831 --> 06:00.365
I wonder what they're gonna put here.

06:00.366 --> 06:01.433
Trader Joe's?

06:01.434 --> 06:04.419
<i>Oh, I would love a Trader Joe's!</i>

06:08.258 --> 06:10.442
Sorry to keep you, I was reading this

06:10.443 --> 06:12.377
<i>Highlights magazine in the waiting room.</i>

06:12.378 --> 06:14.779
Do you see any differences
between these two pictures?

06:14.780 --> 06:16.748
Oh, the pie has a wedge removed.

06:16.749 --> 06:18.450
Yes, yes.

06:18.451 --> 06:20.385
Dr. Hartman, were you
able to tell anything

06:20.386 --> 06:21.653
